From: Tracero project
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt Navigation2 RViz frames to TurtleBot3 Burger
Upstream-Base: ed3521af40f2f73711aace307853bbf125583418

The upstream RViz configuration lists Waffle camera and split rear caster
frames. Tracero's verified Humble simulation uses Burger, whose description
publishes a single caster_back_link and no camera frames.

diff --git a/turtlebot3_navigation2/rviz/tb3_navigation2.rviz b/turtlebot3_navigation2/rviz/tb3_navigation2.rviz
index 0b8a5a4..7b9ae47 100644
--- a/turtlebot3_navigation2/rviz/tb3_navigation2.rviz
+++ b/turtlebot3_navigation2/rviz/tb3_navigation2.rviz
@@ -87,19 +87,7 @@ Visualization Manager:
           Value: true
         base_scan:
           Value: true
-        camera_depth_frame:
-          Value: true
-        camera_depth_optical_frame:
-          Value: true
-        camera_link:
-          Value: true
-        camera_rgb_frame:
-          Value: true
-        camera_rgb_optical_frame:
-          Value: true
-        caster_back_left_link:
-          Value: true
-        caster_back_right_link:
+        caster_back_link:
           Value: true
         imu_link:
           Value: true
